  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836064",
      "title": "Introducing Tailwind CSS For React App Styling",
      "sourceHash": "48dbd1e2c1849b2995a7462f77e2f0e68180ee57698136a278825c870c6775a0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 3.09,
          "en": "Now to conclude this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.09,
          "end": 6.57,
          "en": "let's explore Tailwind CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.57,
          "end": 9.42,
          "en": "Another extremely popular solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.42,
          "end": 11.82,
          "en": "for styling web apps in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.82,
          "end": 14.79,
          "en": "not just React apps, that turns out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.79,
          "end": 17.643,
          "en": "to work really well with React though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.54,
          "end": 23.22,
          "en": "Now Tailwind CSS is a CSS framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.22,
          "end": 26.79,
          "en": "that can be used in any web project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.79,
          "end": 30.9,
          "en": "It's not focused on React or anything like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.9,
          "end": 34.92,
          "en": "but it works really well with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.92,
          "end": 38.31,
          "en": "And what you can see there, is that Tailwind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.31,
          "end": 43.08,
          "en": "is all about adding tiny utility CSS classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.08,
          "end": 45.45,
          "en": "like the classes you're seeing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.45,
          "end": 50.45,
          "en": "to HTML elements to apply styles step by step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.79,
          "end": 53.913,
          "en": "and therefore then style the overall component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.96,
          "end": 58.71,
          "en": "In addition, Tailwind also sets up some base styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.71,
          "end": 61.5,
          "en": "that will affect the overall document,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.5,
          "end": 64.74,
          "en": "but the main idea behind Tailwind really",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.74,
          "end": 68.82,
          "en": "is to add these tiny utility classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.82,
          "end": 71.94,
          "en": "And when you see this for the first time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.94,
          "end": 75.81,
          "en": "this can look pretty intimidating and ugly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.81,
          "end": 78.9,
          "en": "After all, you're going to add a lot of CSS classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.9,
          "end": 80.553,
          "en": "into your JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.53999999999999,
          "end": 84.18,
          "en": "But as you'll see in this demo project here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.18,
          "end": 86.52,
          "en": "it's actually not too bad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.52,
          "end": 90.09,
          "en": "And for many developers working with Tailwind CSS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.09,
          "end": 92.28,
          "en": "is actually pretty convenient,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.28,
          "end": 97.22999999999999,
          "en": "because you don't need to know CSS in order to use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.22999999999999,
          "end": 101.34,
          "en": "That's the idea behind CSS frameworks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 101.34,
          "end": 105.72,
          "en": "Now to use Tailwind CSS, we can go to the docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 105.72,
          "end": 108.47999999999999,
          "en": "on the official Tailwind CSS website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.47999999999999,
          "end": 111.57300000000001,
          "en": "and then there under installation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.59,
          "end": 114.93,
          "en": "you should click on Framework Guides",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.93,
          "end": 119.03999999999999,
          "en": "and there Vite, or you simply use the link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.03999999999999,
          "end": 121.56,
          "en": "you find attached to this lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.56,
          "end": 124.35,
          "en": "Speaking of that, attached to this lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.35,
          "end": 128.64,
          "en": "you also find a link to a new CodeSandbox project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.64,
          "end": 132.33,
          "en": "that already has Tailwind CSS set up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 132.33,
          "end": 135.54,
          "en": "so that you don't need to do it manually there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.54,
          "end": 138.32999999999998,
          "en": "But for the local project, you should go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.32999999999998,
          "end": 140.43,
          "en": "through these setup steps here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.43,
          "end": 144.09,
          "en": "for CodeSandbox simply use the updated Sandbox link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.09,
          "end": 145.353,
          "en": "which you find attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.49,
          "end": 149.22,
          "en": "So in the local project we can skip the first step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.22,
          "end": 151.38,
          "en": "because we already have a project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.38,
          "end": 154.05,
          "en": "but we now have to run these two commands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.05,
          "end": 157.8,
          "en": "to install the Tailwind CSS package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.8,
          "end": 161.19,
          "en": "and some other packages it may require,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.19,
          "end": 163.74,
          "en": "and to initialize it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.74,
          "end": 167.19,
          "en": "The exact commands you see here may change over time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.19,
          "end": 170.223,
          "en": "and you can simply execute the commands you do see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.75,
          "end": 173.91,
          "en": "So you should quit your development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.91,
          "end": 176.79,
          "en": "and run these two commands to install Tailwind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.79,
          "end": 178.563,
          "en": "and initialize it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180,
          "end": 181.11,
          "en": "And once you did that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.11,
          "end": 184.293,
          "en": "you'll see that some new configuration files were added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.19,
          "end": 187.02,
          "en": "Now in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.02,
          "end": 190.41,
          "en": "I'll just get you started with Tailwind CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.41,
          "end": 193.05,
          "en": "This is not a Tailwind CSS course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.05,
          "end": 195.27,
          "en": "and therefore we will not explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.27,
          "end": 197.57999999999998,
          "en": "how you could configure Tailwind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 197.57999999999998,
          "end": 200.253,
          "en": "and all the features it offers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.48,
          "end": 202.68,
          "en": "Instead you should use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 202.68,
          "end": 205.77,
          "en": "the official Tailwind CSS documentation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 205.77,
          "end": 208.74,
          "en": "or some dedicated Tailwind CSS course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 208.74,
          "end": 210.66,
          "en": "if you wanna learn more about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 210.66,
          "end": 212.523,
          "en": "Here we're just getting started.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.78,
          "end": 215.85,
          "en": "And speaking of that, the next step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.85,
          "end": 218.61,
          "en": "is to tweak one of these config files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 218.61,
          "end": 222.963,
          "en": "by overriding the content entry in there with this entry.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.94,
          "end": 227.25,
          "en": "Again, this may change over time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.25,
          "end": 230.52,
          "en": "and therefore when you're following along in your project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.52,
          "end": 233.82,
          "en": "you might see a different step on the Tailwind website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.82,
          "end": 236.37,
          "en": "at the point of time you are following along,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 236.37,
          "end": 240.123,
          "en": "but right now I need to tweak the config as shown here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.55,
          "end": 245.43,
          "en": "And then as a last step pretty much,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 245.43,
          "end": 249.76,
          "en": "we should copy these three statements here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 251.1,
          "end": 253.38,
          "en": "into the index CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 253.38,
          "end": 256.2,
          "en": "And for that I'll actually first copy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.2,
          "end": 258.69,
          "en": "the existing index CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.69,
          "end": 262.29,
          "en": "and rename it to index-old CSS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.29,
          "end": 264.003,
          "en": "so that I still have that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 265.08,
          "end": 269.07,
          "en": "And then delete everything in the remaining index CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 269.07,
          "end": 272.553,
          "en": "and add these three statements here into it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.05,
          "end": 276.063,
          "en": "These are required by Tailwind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 277.40999999999997,
          "end": 279.24,
          "en": "And with that, that's all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 279.24,
          "end": 281.15999999999997,
          "en": "Now, if I run NPM run dev,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 281.15999999999997,
          "end": 284.67,
          "en": "this project will use Tailwind CSS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 284.67,
          "end": 288.36,
          "en": "and therefore, since I renamed the old CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 288.36,
          "end": 292.11,
          "en": "and I'm not importing that renamed file anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 292.11,
          "end": 295.26,
          "en": "as a result, if you visit the website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.26,
          "end": 298.74,
          "en": "you will see that it basically broke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 298.74,
          "end": 300.483,
          "en": "at least to some extent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 301.95,
          "end": 303.48,
          "en": "The header didn't break",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 303.48,
          "end": 306.3,
          "en": "and the input and labels and this button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 306.3,
          "end": 309.06,
          "en": "also still look decent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.06,
          "end": 311.67,
          "en": "because I'm using styled components there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 311.67,
          "end": 314.04,
          "en": "but we're now also going to change that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 314.04,
          "end": 316.533,
          "en": "and instead switch to Tailwind CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 317.94,
          "end": 321,
          "en": "And as I mentioned before, the core idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 321,
          "end": 324.39,
          "en": "behind Tailwind CSS simply is that you add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 324.39,
          "end": 329.39,
          "en": "those tiny utility CSS classes to your elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 329.43,
          "end": 333.72,
          "en": "to change their look, to apply predefined CSS rules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 333.72,
          "end": 336.57,
          "en": "that were defined by the Tailwind team",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 336.57,
          "end": 340.173,
          "en": "and that are available through these utility classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 341.34000000000003,
          "end": 343.95,
          "en": "Therefore, here in this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 343.95,
          "end": 347.46,
          "en": "we can, for example, start by removing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 347.46,
          "end": 350.25,
          "en": "this styled header code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 350.25,
          "end": 352.443,
          "en": "and switching back to a regular header,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 354.93,
          "end": 357.93,
          "en": "and getting rid of that styled import here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 357.93,
          "end": 359.253,
          "en": "and this import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 361.41,
          "end": 364.44,
          "en": "And therefore of course the header is broken now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 364.44,
          "end": 367.743,
          "en": "and we can now start adding these utility classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 369.21,
          "end": 371.73,
          "en": "And for that I'll add the class name prop again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 371.73,
          "end": 372.9,
          "en": "on the header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 372.9,
          "end": 375.84,
          "en": "And now here I'm getting some nice auto completion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 375.84,
          "end": 379.293,
          "en": "for these Tailwind classes, which is pretty convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 380.13,
          "end": 382.923,
          "en": "I'm getting these here in Visual Studio Code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 385.29,
          "end": 389.68,
          "en": "because I installed the Tailwind CSS IntelliSense extension",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 390.75,
          "end": 392.94,
          "en": "which I do recommend installing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 392.94,
          "end": 395.73,
          "en": "It's published by the Tailwind team itself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 395.73,
          "end": 397.8,
          "en": "and it really simplifies the process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 397.8,
          "end": 399.33,
          "en": "of working with Tailwind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 399.33,
          "end": 402.24,
          "en": "since you get Tailwind class name suggestions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 402.24,
          "end": 404.01,
          "en": "and you therefore don't have to look up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 404.01,
          "end": 406.263,
          "en": "all the class names in the official docs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 408.09000000000003,
          "end": 410.37,
          "en": "which is the alternative though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 410.37,
          "end": 412.92,
          "en": "If you dive into those docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 412.92,
          "end": 416.34000000000003,
          "en": "you cannot just learn more about the general core concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 416.34000000000003,
          "end": 419.15999999999997,
          "en": "and how to configure and customize Tailwind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 419.15999999999997,
          "end": 420.54,
          "en": "but you can also learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 420.54,
          "end": 423.033,
          "en": "about the different things you can style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 423.93,
          "end": 427.14,
          "en": "For example, how you can use Flexbox with Tailwind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 427.14,
          "end": 429.42,
          "en": "by adding the flex class to the container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 429.42,
          "end": 431.61,
          "en": "which should create a Flexbox",
          "zh": ""
